{"id": "EUVD-2026-86979", "enisaUuid": "43f3cf4f-fadb-3ed9-bda5-1bc31b445c77", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/gud: validate GUD_ROTATION_0 is present in supported rotations\n\nThe rotation argument to drm_plane_create_rotation_property() is set to\nDRM_MODE_ROTATE_0, and the device reported rotation bitmask is used as\nthe supported_rotations argument. The driver never validates that\nGUD_ROTATION_0 is present, so a device that omits it from its\nGUD_PROPERTY_ROTATION triggers the\nWARN_ON(rotation & ~supported_rotations) in\ndrm_plane_create_rotation_property()\n\nFix this by skipping the creation of rotation property if the device\ndoesn't have the GUD_ROTATION_0 bit", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:36:21", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:54:42", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce7da178f1af4e9cbac4d0440c4002785546bfb5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/962cdf2eedb2708eb99c25ffb56c6d6981d41ed6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2cd682324b889011874cf844b7c7efa97c97296", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/876b33d8a9a00e9d4bbcbb7f55ad2c05974850de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cb732d027aa18e1fcf9d2797f47d20b179ebc59c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98148", "GHSA-pfp2-jmv8-4pwj"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0950170e-5dc2-3788-9cb3-d1831de1baeb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "40e1a70b4aedf2859a1829991b48ef0ebe650bf2 <876b33d8a9a00e9d4bbcbb7f55ad2c05974850de"}, {"id": "1cac272a-cd27-3e11-a229-1b0a2e7106c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "40e1a70b4aedf2859a1829991b48ef0ebe650bf2 <cb732d027aa18e1fcf9d2797f47d20b179ebc59c"}, {"id": "2fd8c1d7-da45-3226-aa51-5d69badbbb20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.13"}, {"id": "69e806cd-5ee4-3ecc-9cdb-771c78904b7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "7094aa30-b3a1-3ece-b706-01fc177f4e56", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "80ca4de2-6bdb-3fb2-a0d8-aaadc541e77b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "88f29a7e-9433-3809-a24f-cb4e77cf543f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9df6f119-82e6-38e5-ba59-78e14c801003", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "acf5cf40-39f7-3dce-aaee-31d69ed5df65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "40e1a70b4aedf2859a1829991b48ef0ebe650bf2 <ce7da178f1af4e9cbac4d0440c4002785546bfb5"}, {"id": "eb6dba52-6e57-3ff7-88a0-2bad6f9e8f94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "40e1a70b4aedf2859a1829991b48ef0ebe650bf2 <b2cd682324b889011874cf844b7c7efa97c97296"}, {"id": "f6b7b688-9ca2-3090-9a6e-d3e66946d3f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "40e1a70b4aedf2859a1829991b48ef0ebe650bf2 <962cdf2eedb2708eb99c25ffb56c6d6981d41ed6"}, {"id": "f9073640-2602-3cc8-a8f4-500617d2d099", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "634ec3d6-bc98-3995-bdfc-a6a2c9aeb888", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}